      "timestamp": 1787159426.3092985
    },
    {
      "id": "usr_igwu0jo7tmt0e1xis",
      "role": "user",
      "text": "*I blink away the fog of sleep, staring up at the ghostly woman as her words sink in. My bare feet press against the frigid stone as I turn toward the north wall, squinting at the high ledge where the ruby key catches the torchlight.*\n\nIf I'm already dead to the world, I guess we have something in common.\n\n*I step closer to the wall, scanning for any loose stones or handholds that might help me reach the ledge.*",
      "image_url": null,
      "timestamp": 1787162145.915264
    },
    {
      "id": "prgm_1310dc49d42440d89e151e7b90f3411a",
      "role": "follower",
      "text": "*The ghost woman's expression softens when you speak, the faintest trace of a sad smile appearing as she nods. She looks down at her translucent hands for a moment, watching them ripple like disturbed water before meeting your eyes again.*\n\nWe share more than that, then. The dead still fight.\n\n*She drifts toward the corner of the cell as you inspect the wall, her presence casting an icy blue glow across the rough-hewn stones. You spot a few protruding blocks near the base — just enough to give you leverage if you time it right. The ledge above is slick with dampness, but the ruby key glints steadily, waiting.*\n\nCareful where you step. The dungeon has seen enough corpses already.",
      "tool_calls": [
        {
          "type": "call",
          "name": "arena_request_skill_check",
